{%- doc -%}
  Echoes what a pro-builder listing includes beyond a plain front print, or
  nothing at all when it is a plain front print.

  Two listings of the same garment can differ only by a back print or by name
  & number, and on a phone that is two tiles with the same photo at different
  prices. Every published product is already tagged with its pricing key
  (..._front vs ..._front_back) and with personalized-back, so the truth was on
  the product all along — it was simply never shown anywhere a shopper looks.

  Name & number takes precedence: it is what is being paid for, and a
  personalized product carries the front_back pricing key anyway, so checking
  it first is what stops both labels applying at once.

  This lives in one snippet because the storefront has two unrelated product
  cards — the theme's block card and the Stella & Sage catalog card — and the
  rule must not drift between them.

  @param {object} product - The product object.

  @example
  {%- capture pro_extra -%}{%- render 'pro-listing-includes', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign pro_extra = pro_extra | strip -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pro_extra = ''

  if product.tags contains 'personalized-back'
    assign pro_extra = 'Name & Number'
  else
    for tag in product.tags
      if tag contains '_front_back'
        assign pro_extra = 'Front & Back'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo pro_extra
-%}
